From b368eb4ea9f2cde97ac0e31074fbac4a10804c21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperVM contributors <supervm@localhost>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 02:06:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] crosvm: seal direct boot memory before enabling KSM

Let Linux request a one-way seal after initialization. Stop all vCPUs,
replace the private RAM slots with read-only registrations, protect the
host mappings, and only then enable KSM. Reject protected writes and
discard; terminate rather than resume after a partial seal.
